      "text": "To determine the type of curve on which all the points \\(\\left( \\frac{t + 1}{t}, \\frac{t - 1}{t} \\right)\\) lie, we start by expressing \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) in terms of \\(t\\):\n\\[x = \\frac{t + 1}{t} = 1 + \\frac{1}{t},\\]\n\\[y = \\frac{t - 1}{t} = 1 - \\frac{1}{t}.\\]\n\nNext, we eliminate the parameter \\(t\\) by finding a relationship between \\(x\\) and \\(y\\). From the expressions for \\(x\\) and \\(y\\), we can solve for \\(t\\) in terms of \\(x\\) and then substitute into the expression for \\(y\\).\n\nFirst, solve for \\(t\\) in terms of \\(x\\):\n\\[x = 1 + \\frac{1}{t},\\]\n\\[x - 1 = \\frac{1}{t},\\]\n\\[t = \\frac{1}{x - 1}.\\]\n\nNow substitute \\(t = \\frac{1}{x - 1}\\) into the expression for \\(y\\):\n\\[y = 1 - \\frac{1}{t} = 1 - \\frac{1}{\\frac{1}{x - 1}} = 1 - (x - 1) = 1 - x + 1 = 2 - x.\\]\n\nThus, we have the relationship:\n\\[y = 2 - x.\\]\n\nThis is the equation of a line. Therefore, all the plotted points lie on a line.\n\nThe correct option is \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
