    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the type of curve on which the points \\((x, y) = \\left( \\frac{t + 1}{t}, \\frac{t - 1}{t} \\right)\\) lie, we will simplify the expressions for \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) and then eliminate \\(t\\) to find a relationship between \\(x\\) and \\(y\\).\n\nGiven:\n\\[ x = \\frac{t + 1}{t} \\]\n\\[ y = \\frac{t - 1}{t} \\]\n\nFirst, let's simplify \\(x\\):\n\\[ x = \\frac{t + 1}{t} = 1 + \\frac{1}{t} \\]\n\nNext, let's simplify \\(y\\):\n\\[ y = \\frac{t - 1}{t} = 1 - \\frac{1}{t} \\]\n\nNow, we have the expressions:\n\\[ x = 1 + \\frac{1}{t} \\]\n\\[ y = 1 - \\frac{1}{t} \\]\n\nWe can solve these equations for \\(\\frac{1}{t}\\) and then eliminate \\(t\\). From the first equation:\n\\[ x - 1 = \\frac{1}{t} \\]\nFrom the second equation:\n\\[ 1 - y = \\frac{1}{t} \\]\n\nEquating the two expressions for \\(\\frac{1}{t}\\):\n\\[ x - 1 = 1 - y \\]\n\\[ x - 1 = 1 - y \\]\n\\[ x + y - 2 = 0 \\]\n\\[ x + y = 2 \\]\n\nThis is the equation of a line. Therefore, all the plotted points \\((x, y)\\) lie on a line.\n\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
